| File | Why it is invalid |
|---|---|
| `INVALID-suite-oldchecker-broken-env.log` | First attempt at "suite with old checker". It ran a hand-built copy whose `ROOT` was still the frozen tree, so `run-exclusive.sh` wrote attempts to `$ROOT/out/...` (the frozen dir) while the copy's `$E` was read for `.latest-run`; every path therefore resolved to `/stages/*.status`, `/harness.log`. Its `14 pass, 21 fail` is an environment artifact, NOT old-checker behaviour. Kept only for the record. |

`mirror-suite-*.log` are the correction: both arms are complete mirrors of the
same layout under `dc-warn`, and the ONLY differences between the arms are the
checker bytes. Their environmental failures are identical in both arms (see
